  "description": "Where a movement puts its past. One pendulum swings under a gallows frame at the head of the open south half; every 25 ms its position is kept together with the time it was taken, and drawn behind the bob at 0.6 m per second of age, so the record recedes down the hall toward the exit. Two limits hold the record: 300 marks and 10 s. A panel on the walk-side post switches the sampler (FINE 25 ms, COARSE 200 ms, STROBE once per measured period) and resets this experiment; a cased readout beside the trail prints the count, the span kept, the interval, the depth rate and the period. The seismograph and the Foucault rig keep other records on other clocks. Structure recovered 2026-09-10: interior 2 = platform, perimeter w, wall_height 3.",
